   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public authorities law, in relation to contracts awarded\nby the Erie county water authority",
    "basePrintNo": "S9098",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9098-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1069, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9098\n\nSPONSOR: KENNEDY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public authorities law, in relation to contracts\nawarded by the Erie county water authority\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill raises the threshold for which the Erie County Water Authority\n(ECWA) must invite sealed bids or proposals for construction-related\nprojects and for equipment, material and supplies.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends section 1069 of the public authorities law, as amended\nby chapter 525 of the laws of 1979.\n\nSection 2 establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrent law establishes that the Erie County Water Authority (ECWA) may\naward a procurement contract involving an expenditure of more than five\nthousand dollars ($5,000) for construction-related projects and for\nequipment, material, and supply only after inviting sealed bids or\nproposals. This statutory threshold has remained the same since 1950.\nFive thousand dollars in 1950 would be the equivalent of fifty-five\nthousand dollars ($55,000) today.\n\nSince 1985, the State Legislature has established the threshold for\nconstruction and purchase contracts for newly created public water,\nauthorities to track the provisions of section 103 of the General Munic-\nipal Law. Section 103 establishes a threshold of twenty thousand dollars\n($20,000) for purchase contracts and thirty-five thousand dollars\n($35,000) for public works contracts. Additionally, other recently\ncreated authorities are required to adhere to General Municipal Law\nsection 101 which requires that when the entire cost of a public work\nproject is estimated to be more than five hundred thousand dollars\n($500,000), then separate specifications and contracts must be let for\ncertain types of projects.\n\nThis bill will allow the Erie County Water Authority the ability to\nraise their current threshold for requiring bids or proposals by corre-\nsponding with the provisions of both General Municipal Law sections 101\nand 103.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
